  "salt": "S7saLFlAvyAJsZi4nZQmEw==",
  "text": "Reid, Thome is a Scottish folkloric figure. The name belongs to a visitor from the Otherworld. Sir Walter Scott passed on a tale from 1576. In it a grey-bearded man in grey clothing and a black bonnet met Bessie Dunlop of Ayrshire. He spoke to her and offered riches. He asked her to give up Christianity in return. She refused, and he vanished. He returned again and again, and she refused him each time. She learned his name, Thome Reid, and that he was a soldier killed in battle. He urged her to come to Fairyland, but she stayed true to her faith. Bessie became a herbalist and took food as her fee. At last the court judged her guilty of witchcraft and burned her.",
